From 9472786c05bfeee2b98be82ab488227ffe1229c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:31:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(linux): build and run the game on linux

The game builds with GCC or Clang against the xboxrecomp runtime's
Linux port: SDL2 for the window, input and audio, and the D3D11
renderer on DXVK-native. The launcher runs on RmlUi's SDL2 and OpenGL 3
backends, with the desktop's sans-serif font and controllers through SDL.

- CMake: a Linux branch for the launcher backend and libraries; the
  translated code keeps MSVC's semantics (no strict aliasing, wrapping
  signed arithmetic, no fused multiply-adds)
- src/mm3_win32.h: windows.h on Windows, the runtime's win32_compat.h
  elsewhere, for the sources that only need the basic Win32 calls
- main.c: the crash report reads the signal's ucontext on x86-64 and
  arm64 Linux
- the teleport debugger stays Windows only; its player update hook does
  not
- recomp_manual.c: a full fence where x86 has _mm_sfence
